The row is still blocked by one c2 register-colouring decision. sub_primitive (priority 58-59) is coloured before mesh_primitive (49), so ours has sub=edi, mesh=ebp, `this` in memory and a 0xAC frame; retail has sub=ebx, mesh=edi, this=ebp and a 0xB0 frame. That one difference shifts the temp registers and slots through the whole function. Things that remain even when the flip is forced:
- frame-slot offsets;
- pass 12/13 (stencil/fill) does not hoist the OS/OF argument pushes the way retail does;
- the case 4/6 jumps into case 7's pixel-shader call;
- case 3 shares its SetupShaderSpotLight call with another case in ours, but has its own in retail.
Under forcing, the best match is 1903-1904 of retail's 2419 instructions.
Best source: differ/00ba2350.cpp (attempt 2's m5, unchanged). r3/h1.cpp adds two FableWin-size-proven helper texts and grades 9548v9632 with 353 hunks.
